WEBVTT

00:00:03.892 --> 00:00:07.902
CANDY CANDY

00:00:10.703 --> 00:00:16.429
Sobakasu nante kinishinai wa.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:23.023
Hana pecha datte datte datte oki ni iri.

00:00:24.151 --> 00:00:27.269
Otenba itazura daisuki,

00:00:27.425 --> 00:00:30.595
Kakekko sukippu daisuki;

00:00:30.749 --> 00:00:35.759
Watashi wa, watashi wa, watashi wa Candy!

00:00:37.204 --> 00:00:43.192
Hitoripocchi de iru to choppiri samishii.

00:00:43.869 --> 00:00:49.768
Sonna toki kou iu no kagami wo mitsumete:

00:00:49.921 --> 00:00:56.181
Waratte, waratte, waratte Candy!

00:00:56.538 --> 00:00:59.279
Nakibeso nante sayonara!

00:00:59.449 --> 00:01:02.702
Nee, Candy Candy!

00:01:12.318 --> 00:01:17.472
Summer school at the shore of a lake.

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:21.861
Summertime is here.

00:01:23.095 --> 00:01:26.892
Candy went to the Summer school in Scotland.

00:01:27.985 --> 00:01:34.753
They say that Edinburgh, a center of Scotland,
is one of the most beautiful places in the world.

00:01:35.396 --> 00:01:40.802
Away from Edinburgh, there is a small
village on the shore of a lake.

00:01:40.837 --> 00:01:43.584
Candy and the others will stay there
during their summer vacation.

00:01:48.661 --> 00:01:50.637
That's the Summer school's church?

00:01:51.317 --> 00:01:53.985
Mr. God followed us even on a summer vacation...

00:01:54.149 --> 00:01:57.905
Can't help it, our school is a religious school.

00:02:01.047 --> 00:02:02.556
Bagpipes!

00:02:02.985 --> 00:02:05.094
There is a festival in the village.

00:02:05.319 --> 00:02:06.659
I wanted to see that!

00:02:06.875 --> 00:02:08.292
Candy, wait!

00:02:37.387 --> 00:02:38.866
The prince on the hill...

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.660
...so this is your homeland?

00:02:49.594 --> 00:02:50.773
Hey! Stop!

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.383
Wait, number 93!

00:02:55.789 --> 00:02:57.576
-It's looking this way!
-I'm afraid!

00:02:58.712 --> 00:03:01.172
Sheep are calm creatures.
There, there.

00:03:03.581 --> 00:03:07.481
-Why did you run away again?!
-Don't be so violent!

00:03:07.652 --> 00:03:10.222
But this thing keeps running away!

00:03:10.507 --> 00:03:13.471
It ran away while you were shearing it?

00:03:14.715 --> 00:03:16.601
You're gonna get some if
you do that again!

00:03:16.636 --> 00:03:17.919
It's probably afraid of cold!

00:03:17.947 --> 00:03:18.917
Afraid of cold?

00:03:19.286 --> 00:03:22.890
So funny of you to say that!
I've never heard of such a thing before!

00:03:24.978 --> 00:03:26.162
What?

00:03:27.134 --> 00:03:29.899
Freckles... that flat nose...

00:03:30.587 --> 00:03:32.700
I remember!
You're Candy!

00:03:32.747 --> 00:03:34.808
Sis, you're Candy, aren't you?

00:03:34.967 --> 00:03:37.323
How come you know my name?

00:03:39.638 --> 00:03:41.147
You look exactly like her!

00:03:41.308 --> 00:03:42.253
Like who?

00:03:42.761 --> 00:03:44.346
Like someone my brother told me about.

00:03:44.966 --> 00:03:46.404
Brother...?

00:03:46.436 --> 00:03:48.867
Teacher! Candy and the others are there!

00:03:49.339 --> 00:03:53.670
What are you doing there?
You'll have some free time later on!

00:03:53.851 --> 00:03:55.764
-Sorry!
-We'll go back rightaway!

00:03:58.053 --> 00:04:02.096
You got her mad!
Now, thanks for nr. 93!

00:04:02.097 --> 00:04:03.939
-Wait up!
-Candy!

00:04:04.883 --> 00:04:08.152
Instead of watching the festivities,
you'd better unpack your luggage!

00:04:08.883 --> 00:04:09.830
Luggage?

00:04:11.176 --> 00:04:12.097
Kurin!

00:04:12.166 --> 00:04:13.382
Now, go!

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.098
I must hurry.

00:04:22.563 --> 00:04:23.920
I totally forgot about you!

00:04:24.995 --> 00:04:25.809
Kurin!

00:04:29.851 --> 00:04:31.212
Sorry, sorry.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:35.357
I was so engrosses in festivities
that I totally forgot about you.

00:04:36.927 --> 00:04:40.059
Sisters will take notice
if you keep growling like that.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:43.301
Will you forgive me if I bring you
something nice for dinner?

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:48.717
Thanks.

00:04:52.764 --> 00:04:56.341
Now, Kurin, your favorite food:
smoked salmon.

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:03.956
Yes!
Come in!

00:05:04.969 --> 00:05:08.098
We have something for Kurin!
This one is from us.

00:05:08.877 --> 00:05:11.259
But you shouldn't have...

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:14.534
We're partially at fault for this, too.
Right, Patty?

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:16.805
Kurin, this is for you.

00:05:18.764 --> 00:05:20.928
But what about that sheep?

00:05:21.484 --> 00:05:24.815
It's probaby sneezing now that all
of its wool is gone.

00:05:26.975 --> 00:05:29.870
By the way, just who was that shepherd boy?

00:05:30.461 --> 00:05:33.440
He said that his older brother knows you.

00:05:34.462 --> 00:05:36.279
-Candy?
-What?

00:05:36.529 --> 00:05:40.402
Maybe the older brother of that boy
is the Prince on the hill!

00:05:41.851 --> 00:05:43.269
You're kidding me!

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:48.204
There's no way that an older brother of
such a naughty kid would be Prince!

00:05:48.205 --> 00:05:51.115
Do you know anyone else in Scotland?

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.538
When you put it that way...

00:05:54.601 --> 00:05:58.327
Alright. I'm going to find him tomorrow
and ask him about this.

00:06:31.536 --> 00:06:33.797
Okay. Looks like this is the only way.

00:06:42.115 --> 00:06:43.574
Got out all right.

00:06:43.609 --> 00:06:44.424
Candy!

00:06:45.634 --> 00:06:47.700
Teacher! Good morning!

00:06:47.928 --> 00:06:48.820
Good morning.

00:06:48.917 --> 00:06:53.818
Candy, before going out for a walk, regulations say
that you have to participate in a morning mass.

00:06:54.477 --> 00:06:56.102
I'll forgive you if you come back.

00:06:56.272 --> 00:06:57.919
Don't break the rules without hesitation.

00:06:58.678 --> 00:06:59.525
Yes!

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:07.468
Seeing the crowds,
Jesus went up on the mountain,

00:07:07.836 --> 00:07:11.232
...and when he sat down
his disciples came to him.

00:07:11.577 --> 00:07:15.635
And he spoke up and taught them, saying:

00:07:15.779 --> 00:07:19.450
Blessed are the poor in spirit...

00:07:21.181 --> 00:07:22.417
-Candy!
-Yes!

00:07:22.755 --> 00:07:24.274
What's the meaning of this?

00:07:25.362 --> 00:07:27.533
Uh, that sheep...

00:07:30.507 --> 00:07:32.011
What sheep?

00:07:32.995 --> 00:07:34.558
Sister, it's true!

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:36.627
It really is!

00:07:40.376 --> 00:07:42.558
Quiet! Everyone, calm down!

00:07:44.281 --> 00:07:45.694
You escaped again?

00:07:46.603 --> 00:07:48.939
You know this sheep?

00:07:49.096 --> 00:07:54.613
Yes, sister! Since it's a bother,
can I go and return it to its owner?

00:07:54.648 --> 00:07:56.216
Yes! Do you know its owner?

00:07:56.636 --> 00:07:58.097
-Yes!
-Candy...

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:00.981
I'll be back soon!

00:08:01.204 --> 00:08:02.431
Don't take too long.

00:08:03.251 --> 00:08:05.493
Okay. Go, go...

00:08:27.844 --> 00:08:29.912
You saved me back there.

00:08:31.291 --> 00:08:35.879
But I'm confused... I don't know the
name of that boy or where he lives...

00:08:39.496 --> 00:08:41.397
I'll ask that old man.

00:08:42.229 --> 00:08:43.371
Mister!

00:08:45.607 --> 00:08:46.914
Can I help you?

00:08:47.203 --> 00:08:49.578
Do you know of a farm that keeps sheep?

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:52.238
A farm that keeps sheep?

00:08:54.419 --> 00:08:56.376
Everyone in this village has sheep.

00:08:56.519 --> 00:08:59.168
Don't you know where that sheep came from?

00:08:59.286 --> 00:09:02.018
I'm sure it was called nr. 93...

00:09:03.859 --> 00:09:05.524
It could be one of Mark's sheep.

00:09:05.817 --> 00:09:06.693
Mark's?

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:09.055
Hey, Mark! Mark!

00:09:10.918 --> 00:09:12.954
What is it?
Huh?

00:09:13.138 --> 00:09:14.148
You!

00:09:15.142 --> 00:09:17.850
Can I help you?
Freckled lady!

00:09:21.137 --> 00:09:24.821
Freckled lady? And I brought
your sheep back to you!

00:09:24.822 --> 00:09:27.439
What? It came back again?

00:09:29.211 --> 00:09:32.796
Nr. 93 didn't run away!
I actually wanted it to run away!

00:09:33.282 --> 00:09:35.104
Shoo! Go away!

00:09:35.305 --> 00:09:36.948
You're free!

00:09:37.181 --> 00:09:38.767
Say, what's the meaning of this?

00:09:38.901 --> 00:09:41.333
It keeps running away from my brother's farm.

00:09:41.727 --> 00:09:44.384
Since it wants to run away so much,
I let it go free!

00:09:44.419 --> 00:09:45.822
Who is your brother?

00:09:46.555 --> 00:09:48.543
Of course, Terry!

00:09:49.031 --> 00:09:50.003
Terry?

00:09:50.766 --> 00:09:52.297
Grandchester's Terry?

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.708
Terrius G. Grandchester!

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:58.003
Then, you're Terry's little brother?

00:09:58.914 --> 00:10:00.361
Call me Mark!

00:10:00.938 --> 00:10:03.160
So that's why you knew about me?

00:10:03.847 --> 00:10:06.885
Bro is a funny guy, he lets me hang around!

00:10:07.044 --> 00:10:09.596
Say, Terry comes to this place?

00:10:10.318 --> 00:10:11.620
He has a mansion here!

00:10:11.621 --> 00:10:14.117
Mark, I'd like you to take me there!

00:10:15.329 --> 00:10:17.672
What about your Summer school?

00:10:18.209 --> 00:10:20.531
Sisters allowed me out.

00:10:20.827 --> 00:10:22.961
-Hop in, then.
-Thanks.

00:10:26.594 --> 00:10:28.041
Can't help it, I guess!

00:10:48.635 --> 00:10:50.735
-Grampa, thanks!
-Thank you!

00:10:53.895 --> 00:10:56.669
I expected nothing less of
Duke Grandchester's mansion!

00:10:58.337 --> 00:10:59.335
Bro!

00:10:59.922 --> 00:11:01.823
So that's Terry's room?

00:11:01.858 --> 00:11:04.290
Bro! Freckles is here!

00:11:04.587 --> 00:11:06.650
Don't call me like that!

00:11:07.187 --> 00:11:08.389
Strange...

00:11:08.819 --> 00:11:11.283
-Maybe he's out?
-Bro!

00:11:15.585 --> 00:11:16.730
Mark!

00:11:17.779 --> 00:11:21.439
Mark, I'll punish you if you keep
calling Master by whistling!

00:11:21.945 --> 00:11:23.275
Lady, good day.

00:11:23.634 --> 00:11:25.947
Welcome to Scotland.

00:11:26.628 --> 00:11:28.899
Mom, bro isn't here?

00:11:29.078 --> 00:11:29.978
Mom?

00:11:30.466 --> 00:11:33.591
Yes, it's my son I've already told you about.

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:37.177
Then, he's not Terry's real brother?

00:11:37.517 --> 00:11:43.025
No way! But master Terry doesn't have a problem
with that since he really likes my son.

00:11:43.026 --> 00:11:45.267
I'm Terry's best friend!

00:11:45.668 --> 00:11:46.722
Mark!

00:11:47.136 --> 00:11:48.800
Uh, is Terry...

00:11:51.411 --> 00:11:54.902
He told me that he doesn't want to see anyone.

00:11:55.083 --> 00:11:56.718
Has something happened?

00:12:02.011 --> 00:12:02.931
Terry...

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:10.872
*Denjin Anime Fansub*
You might have wondered why the bad picture quality.
You see, Candy was never released on DVD and only
saw a limited VHS edition in Japan. By fansubbing
this lo-res TV/VHS version, we want to give you the
incentive to buy legitimate Japanese DVDs once they
are released. You are free to extract our softsubs
and apply them to your LEGITIMATE, original DVDs
you will purchase directly from Toei/Japan. If that's not
the spirit of fansubbing, I really don't know what is.

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:18.098
This melody...

00:12:18.251 --> 00:12:22.359
It's a Scottish poem,
Auld lang syne.

00:12:22.562 --> 00:12:24.004
Auld lang syne?

00:12:26.359 --> 00:12:29.142
It's a song we sing
when we part from someone.

00:12:29.308 --> 00:12:30.591
Part from someone?

00:12:50.913 --> 00:12:51.996
Terry!

00:12:53.496 --> 00:12:55.742
It's me! Candy!

00:12:56.005 --> 00:12:58.289
If you're there, let me see you!

00:13:05.024 --> 00:13:07.074
Just what happened to him?

00:13:08.465 --> 00:13:13.258
He said he wanted to be alone for a while.
He even gave me a few days off.

00:13:13.868 --> 00:13:15.033
Alone?

00:13:15.205 --> 00:13:18.484
All guys want to be alone sometimes!

00:13:18.677 --> 00:13:19.740
You're rude!

00:13:19.775 --> 00:13:24.449
-And women always want to cackle together!
-Mark!

00:13:31.776 --> 00:13:33.740
Isn't that the same sheep?

00:13:34.022 --> 00:13:37.294
Annie, Candice was supposed to return the sheep,
so what happened?

00:13:37.407 --> 00:13:38.098
Yes...

00:13:38.659 --> 00:13:40.208
She's so much trouble...

00:13:45.465 --> 00:13:48.753
You got in just a right moment.
I'll prepare a lunch for you.

00:13:49.742 --> 00:13:53.518
-Mark, get the cheese from the cellar!
-Yes!

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:56.983
-Our place is a bit dingy, does it surprise you?
-Not at all!

00:13:57.809 --> 00:14:00.890
Your place looks exactly like
Pony's home where I grew up.

00:14:01.193 --> 00:14:03.820
-Miss, you lived in such a house?
-Yes!

00:14:03.895 --> 00:14:05.631
Until I was about Mark's age.

00:14:05.838 --> 00:14:08.490
-So that's why you're a tomboy!
-Mark!

00:14:09.386 --> 00:14:12.462
-Here! I made this cheese!
-Looks tasty!

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:17.712
Looks tasty? It's doesn't just look that way,
it actually tastes great!

00:14:17.877 --> 00:14:18.792
I know.

00:14:19.389 --> 00:14:22.532
Mark, while your mother was working in London...

00:14:22.983 --> 00:14:26.596
...he took good care of this house!
Right, Mark?

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:28.974
I'm glad you weren't alone.

00:14:29.259 --> 00:14:30.725
It's because Dad was with me!

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:32.027
With your father?

00:14:32.161 --> 00:14:33.113
Over there!

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:41.709
Tartan check?

00:14:44.044 --> 00:14:47.022
His father used to make them.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:51.089
He was the best craftsman in the entire village...

00:14:52.128 --> 00:14:53.575
So warm!

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:57.759
I'll continue in my father's footsteps!

00:14:58.234 --> 00:14:59.525
Do your best then!

00:15:00.576 --> 00:15:07.056
The Prince's kilt... maybe it was
made of tartan check Mark's father made?

00:15:09.015 --> 00:15:10.846
Is something wrong?

00:15:11.254 --> 00:15:14.648
No, I just got a feeling as if I
returned to my homeland.

00:15:15.719 --> 00:15:19.296
-Now, your soup is getting cold!
-Okay! Let's eat!

00:15:25.909 --> 00:15:30.618
You're the first student of Summer school
to go missing for eight hours!

00:15:31.337 --> 00:15:34.337
I didn't realize it until it got dark...

00:15:34.697 --> 00:15:35.765
Here...

00:15:36.873 --> 00:15:38.154
What is that?

00:15:38.234 --> 00:15:41.167
Cheese. I want to give it to you as a present.

00:15:41.358 --> 00:15:46.641
My! You're also the first student
to bring cheese as a present...

00:15:50.532 --> 00:15:52.420
-Candy!
-They scolded you?

00:15:53.215 --> 00:15:55.770
Stear and Archie arrived during the day.

00:15:56.164 --> 00:15:57.210
Both of them?

00:15:57.776 --> 00:16:02.148
Candy, Aunt Elroy rented a nearby mansion.

00:16:03.079 --> 00:16:07.121
-Then, it means that Neil and Eliza are here too?
-Yes.

00:16:07.826 --> 00:16:11.663
Oh boy, I have to look at their faces
even here in Scotland...

00:16:14.141 --> 00:16:15.715
Stear borrowed it to us!

00:16:16.341 --> 00:16:18.522
It's dark outside, you won't see a thing.

00:16:20.524 --> 00:16:23.712
Terry's mansion is on the other side.

00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:28.923
There it is!

00:16:30.037 --> 00:16:33.072
Lights are on
in Terry's room only.

00:16:34.146 --> 00:16:35.323
-Candy?
-Eh?

00:16:36.204 --> 00:16:37.363
What are you looking at?

00:16:38.611 --> 00:16:39.673
It's nothing!

00:16:40.127 --> 00:16:44.766
Candy, Stear and Archie promised they'd take
us for a boat ride during tomorrow's free time!

00:16:45.161 --> 00:16:46.519
Archie is going to come!

00:16:47.679 --> 00:16:48.542
I see.

00:16:49.671 --> 00:16:51.315
Aren't you glad, Candy?

00:16:51.711 --> 00:16:53.773
Of course I am!

00:16:53.876 --> 00:16:56.752
Say, let's call it a day.
I'm so tired.

00:16:57.434 --> 00:16:59.486
Okay. Good night!

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:36.067
A woman?

00:17:57.569 --> 00:17:58.802
Do you best, Stear!

00:17:58.915 --> 00:18:01.318
-Archie, don't give up!
-Like I was going to!

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:07.644
-Archie, I'm running behind! Take it easy there!
-That's how things are, bro!

00:18:09.691 --> 00:18:10.679
Terry...

00:18:13.808 --> 00:18:14.968
We won, Annie!

00:18:15.062 --> 00:18:19.213
-Candy, if you're not afraid, wanna ride the boat?
-Come on!

00:18:19.351 --> 00:18:21.116
It's so fun!

00:18:21.433 --> 00:18:24.099
It's okay, I'm going for a walk.

00:18:27.929 --> 00:18:28.953
Candy?

00:18:29.842 --> 00:18:30.966
Something happened to her?

00:18:30.967 --> 00:18:37.076
Yes. She's been acting strange since last night.
She keeps watching that mansion with binoculars...

00:18:46.309 --> 00:18:50.449
Just who was the person in
Terry's room last night?

00:18:57.820 --> 00:18:59.813
It's... Eleanor Baker?

00:19:02.041 --> 00:19:04.210
It's Terry's real mother.

00:19:11.439 --> 00:19:13.352
Then, the shadow I saw last night...

00:19:30.553 --> 00:19:31.622
Uh...

00:19:36.392 --> 00:19:38.696
Did she come from America to see Terry?

00:19:42.833 --> 00:19:44.397
Hey! Wait!

00:19:44.432 --> 00:19:45.291
Wait!

00:19:45.449 --> 00:19:46.608
Wait!
Ow!

00:19:50.472 --> 00:19:51.501
Terry!

00:19:54.053 --> 00:19:55.205
Catch it!

00:19:59.223 --> 00:20:01.523
He was sulking yesterday, and now...

00:20:02.065 --> 00:20:03.198
Hey! Wait!

00:20:03.773 --> 00:20:05.575
Hey! It's here!

00:20:05.853 --> 00:20:07.646
Hello, Freckled Tarzan.

00:20:08.211 --> 00:20:09.839
Freckled Tarzan?

00:20:14.192 --> 00:20:15.863
Terry, over there I...

00:20:17.238 --> 00:20:18.764
Uh, over there...

00:20:18.919 --> 00:20:21.328
What, you tripped on purpose again?

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:23.181
Terry!

00:20:24.797 --> 00:20:26.481
Don't tell anyone about that woman.

00:20:27.983 --> 00:20:29.505
Terry, last night...

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:32.273
Last night, my brother stayed at home!

00:20:32.358 --> 00:20:33.570
-Right?
-Yeah.

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:36.434
But... you two didn't meet?

00:20:38.191 --> 00:20:40.532
What nonsense is that?

00:20:40.591 --> 00:20:42.682
-It ran away again! Bro!
-Alright, catch it!

00:20:43.675 --> 00:20:45.102
Bro, quickly!

00:20:46.176 --> 00:20:47.638
Alright, don't let it go.

00:20:49.116 --> 00:20:51.470
I thought you let that sheep go free?

00:20:51.505 --> 00:20:53.209
Yeah, but I changed my mind.

00:20:53.318 --> 00:20:55.126
-Mark! Get the shears!
-Ok.

00:20:58.259 --> 00:21:01.436
Terry, I just saw your mother over there.

00:21:02.304 --> 00:21:04.111
I'm sure she came to see you.

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:08.196
It's already noon, but you're still dreaming?

00:21:08.571 --> 00:21:10.700
But, she came all the way from America...

00:21:11.039 --> 00:21:13.078
My mother is in London.

00:21:13.863 --> 00:21:16.609
So Eleanor Baker isn't your real mother?

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:18.679
Wow, I really did it!

00:21:18.714 --> 00:21:19.846
What is so funny?

00:21:20.632 --> 00:21:22.591
You actually bought that story?

00:21:22.767 --> 00:21:24.079
So that was a lie?

00:21:24.337 --> 00:21:25.249
Of course.

00:21:26.165 --> 00:21:27.302
Bro, the shears!

00:21:27.498 --> 00:21:29.513
Alright! Now, let's get to work!

00:21:29.754 --> 00:21:31.424
Get ready, Eleanor!

00:21:31.701 --> 00:21:32.778
Eleanor?

00:21:33.738 --> 00:21:36.532
The number was stupid, so my bro
made up this name!

00:21:36.719 --> 00:21:39.553
Eleanor, I'm going to tear that disguise off you.

00:21:49.481 --> 00:21:50.708
Terry...

00:21:51.707 --> 00:21:55.877
It's your duty to let humans protect themselves
with this warm wool of yours.

00:21:57.646 --> 00:22:01.963
The same way a mother has a duty to
protect her child with her kind heart!

00:22:03.569 --> 00:22:06.110
If you can't do that, you're not a sheep!

00:22:06.289 --> 00:22:07.566
...nor a mother!

00:22:09.553 --> 00:22:10.798
Do you understand, Eleanor?

00:22:17.497 --> 00:22:19.511
While Terry was saying these words,

00:22:19.891 --> 00:22:27.553
...Candy remembered Mark's house, where she saw
a poor mother and her son helping each other.

00:22:27.935 --> 00:22:34.930
To be continued...

00:22:41.074 --> 00:22:49.556
Ashita wa doko kara
umarete kuru no

00:22:49.885 --> 00:22:59.014
Watashi wa, ashita ga,
ashita ga suki.

00:22:59.718 --> 00:23:08.375
Suteki na koto ga
ari sore

00:23:08.535 --> 00:23:17.971
Watashi wa, ashita ga
ashita ga suki.

00:23:18.348 --> 00:23:26.717
Kirakira hikaru
Kaze no mukou de

00:23:26.999 --> 00:23:37.879
Ano hito ga watashi wo
Watashi wo yondeiru - -

00:23:38.272 --> 00:23:49.273
Candy, Candy, Candy, Candy.

00:23:49.919 --> 00:23:52.950
*Next episode*
The link between a mother and a child.

00:23:53.562 --> 00:23:57.874
Grandchester's mansion stands
at the shore of a beautiful lake.

00:23:58.715 --> 00:24:03.213
One morning, I saw a very
sad looking Terry's mother...

00:24:03.398 --> 00:24:06.835
...and Terry who kept looking away
on the other side of the fence.

00:24:07.582 --> 00:24:09.807
But then I found a book.

00:24:10.335 --> 00:24:14.265
It was a very precious thing
that connected Terry and his mother!

00:24:14.713 --> 00:24:18.151
Next time on Candy Candy,
"The link between a mother and a child."

00:24:18.152 --> 00:24:19.907
The picture quality will be really bad,
so don't look forward to it!
